*.log
# ...except the frozen private-state fixture's LevelDB write-ahead log, which is
# the only file in that store holding the encrypted state. Without it a fresh
# clone gets a store that opens but returns nothing, and the consuming test
# reports an envelope break that never happened.
!testkit-js/testkit-js/src/fixtures/hf/pre-fork-private-state-store/store/*.log
# LevelDB's runtime files are NOT part of that fixture, and none of them matches
# the `*.log` rule above. `LOG` carries wall-clock timestamps, so committing one
# would freeze a single machine's run log into a store whose whole value is byte
# determinism -- and the digest gate would then bless it, because the digest is
# defined by the bytes present rather than by an expected file set.
testkit-js/testkit-js/src/fixtures/hf/pre-fork-private-state-store/store/LOCK
testkit-js/testkit-js/src/fixtures/hf/pre-fork-private-state-store/store/LOG
testkit-js/testkit-js/src/fixtures/hf/pre-fork-private-state-store/store/LOG.old
